      "message": "NIT:\n\nThis file lives under docs, which is not covered by the gap this commit closes: npm run lint is now eslint src tests (not docs), and format-code.sh only runs npm run lint. So reformatting config.js does not close any CI lint gap — it is a cosmetic reflow that would only ever be enforced incidentally via lint-staged on a future edit.\n\nWhy: Mixing an unrelated cosmetic reindent into a \"close the lint gaps\" change slightly widens the diff beyond its stated purpose — a common maintainer objection on OpenBMC/Gerrit. Impact is low because the commit body explicitly discloses it (\"Prettier also reindents docs/.vuepress/config.js…\"), so this is not blocking.\n\nRecommendation: Acceptable as-is given the disclosure; optionally split the config.js reindent into its own trivial commit so the tooling/doc change stays self-contained. No code change required",
